WEBVTT

00:00:01.250 --> 00:00:02.960
(Episode 32)

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:05.290
Since you get it, does that mean I don't have to do the transplant?

00:00:07.130 --> 00:00:09.659
Oh, my. Eun Oh.

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:11.800
I know you sought me out on purpose from the very beginning.

00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:15.270
It was no coincidence. Everything, from the very beginning until now...

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:17.840
I know you planned it all, so...

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:20.810
don't bother making excuses. Just leave.

00:00:24.610 --> 00:00:26.150
That son of yours...

00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:29.350
is never getting my liver.

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:33.590
What are you talking about?

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:46.700
(National ID Card, Name: Ko Seong Hui)

00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:50.900
You abandoned me.

00:00:59.710 --> 00:01:00.910
How did you get this?

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:07.290
Don't lose all hope.

00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:10.960
This recording is more than enough evidence.

00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:14.790
You were recording that?

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:17.830
Just in case.

00:01:20.570 --> 00:01:21.570
Excuse me.

00:01:24.470 --> 00:01:28.010
My mom salvaged some things from the ashes.

00:01:28.070 --> 00:01:29.740
She says they're in a box in the storage room.

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:31.750
Would you like to go through it?

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:35.080
Yes.

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:56.870
(National ID Card)

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:09.020
(National ID Card, Name: Ko Seong Hui)

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:12.549
You deliberately approached me and got close to lower my guard.

00:02:12.550 --> 00:02:13.990
For months, you deceived me.

00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:15.390
I will never forgive you.

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:20.230
- Eun Oh, please, just hear me out. - How can you be so cruel?

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:22.430
How could you do something like that?

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:24.430
How could a mother...

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:27.200
make a fool of and deceive the daughter she abandoned?

00:02:27.470 --> 00:02:30.470
You should've come and begged me. You should have just asked.

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:35.540
But I won't even go there.

00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:38.780
What?

00:02:40.310 --> 00:02:41.850
Even though you abandoned me,

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:46.090
you did something you'd never do if you saw me as your real daughter.

00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:47.850
So why bother resenting you?

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:50.060
You'll just make excuses anyway.

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:55.200
The reason I won't do the liver transplant...

00:02:55.660 --> 00:02:59.670
is because it's the worst punishment I can give you.

00:03:01.430 --> 00:03:04.370
My liver seems to be the one thing you desperately need,

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:06.710
and you came to take it from me. That's why you can't have it.

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:09.240
Aren't you something.

00:03:11.810 --> 00:03:13.510
You've said your piece.

00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:15.850
So can I talk now?

00:03:16.520 --> 00:03:18.820
- No. - I didn't abandon you.

00:03:20.190 --> 00:03:23.020
So you found this and just assumed I abandoned you?

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:28.089
After your father died, I couldn't raise you both alone,

00:03:28.090 --> 00:03:29.600
so I left you there temporarily.

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:32.069
I couldn't afford to take you both,

00:03:32.070 --> 00:03:33.730
so I came back for your brother first.

00:03:34.830 --> 00:03:36.270
When I went back for you,

00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:38.610
the orphanage had burned down.

00:03:40.310 --> 00:03:43.580
I tracked you down to the orphanage in Cheongju,

00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:49.250
but you had been fully adopted and were gone.

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:56.120
If it had been a regular adoption, I would have tried to get you back.

00:03:56.660 --> 00:03:58.330
But they said it was a full adoption.

00:03:59.930 --> 00:04:00.930
And what's more?

00:04:01.330 --> 00:04:03.400
By a very wealthy family with their own business.

00:04:05.470 --> 00:04:07.730
They had accepted you as their own flesh and blood.

00:04:09.670 --> 00:04:11.140
So I let you go.

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:14.370
It seemed you'd have a better life than I could provide.

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:16.340
I gritted my teeth and walked away.

00:04:18.980 --> 00:04:22.120
After all that, how could I show up and ask for a suitability test?

00:04:22.180 --> 00:04:23.550
How could I have the nerve?

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:27.690
The fact that I found this copy of your ID...

00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:29.960
means I know everything. I heard it all!

00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:31.590
Heard it all? What did you hear?

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:33.990
That I came back and only took your brother?

00:04:35.230 --> 00:04:39.100
That was for his ear surgery. I told you. I went back for you!

00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:41.100
I said you'd already been adopted.

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:45.040
Stop it. Please, just stop with the lies!

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:48.580
The reason I approached you without telling you who I was...

00:04:48.940 --> 00:04:51.280
is because there was a good chance you wouldn't be a match.

00:04:52.850 --> 00:04:54.510
And besides, I wanted to see you.

00:04:55.050 --> 00:04:56.880
I wanted to see how my daughter had grown up.

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:00.320
But once I actually met you,

00:05:01.290 --> 00:05:03.090
I just couldn't bring myself to ask you to get tested.

00:05:05.330 --> 00:05:06.990
And while that was happening, as you know...

00:05:07.830 --> 00:05:09.560
We found a donor, but they backed out.

00:05:11.970 --> 00:05:13.000
I...

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:16.340
I wasn't going to tell you I was your mother, ever.

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:18.670
Because I knew it would hurt you.

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:22.110
I thought we could just be like close friends.

00:05:22.540 --> 00:05:24.780
I hoped I could stay in your life like that forever.

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:29.320
But then, the donor fell through.

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:31.790
So I had no choice but to turn to you.

00:05:32.090 --> 00:05:33.650
Why turn to me?

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:36.220
I thought you said you didn't know if I'd be a match.

00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:40.890
No, that's a lie. You knew all along.

00:05:41.930 --> 00:05:45.330
You had me take the suitability test under the guise of a health checkup.

00:05:47.170 --> 00:05:48.230
No...

00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:50.670
What are you talking about?

00:05:52.070 --> 00:05:54.239
I went back to the hospital where we had our checkup...

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:55.440
and reviewed my records.

00:05:56.980 --> 00:05:57.980
I...

00:05:58.380 --> 00:06:01.850
had an MRI and an abdominal CT scan, but they said there were no records.

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:03.820
I wonder who could've been involved.

00:06:04.980 --> 00:06:07.120
Hospital Director Yoon Seong Mo and you, Ms. Ko Seong Hui.

00:06:08.350 --> 00:06:11.490
Turns out you're both members of the same volunteer group abroad.

00:06:13.090 --> 00:06:14.930
How much does she know?

00:06:19.800 --> 00:06:21.530
Should I file a formal complaint?

00:06:22.570 --> 00:06:23.770
With the hospital,

00:06:24.070 --> 00:06:26.210
and look into whether a donor really did back out.

00:06:31.410 --> 00:06:32.510
No, why on earth...

00:06:33.380 --> 00:06:36.120
Why would you even think something so horrible?

00:06:36.520 --> 00:06:41.020
- You should've asked. I'll explain. - Oh, please.

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:46.330
Stop it. I said, stop! Are you even human?

00:06:52.970 --> 00:06:55.340
Someone's life is on the line.

00:06:59.110 --> 00:07:00.210
Here we go again.

00:07:03.110 --> 00:07:04.380
Please, save your brother.

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:06.980
He's your older brother.

00:07:07.850 --> 00:07:09.650
He's your son, not mine.

00:07:11.020 --> 00:07:12.550
I'm not your daughter.

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:14.520
What older brother? I don't have one.

00:07:20.260 --> 00:07:22.160
Ms. Ji, is your guest leaving now?

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:24.000
Yes.

00:07:27.700 --> 00:07:28.900
This way, ma'am.

00:07:29.900 --> 00:07:31.170
Who are these people?

00:07:31.600 --> 00:07:34.010
She seems more like an intruder than a visitor.

00:07:34.270 --> 00:07:35.940
It's time for her to leave.

00:07:36.580 --> 00:07:38.040
Please escort her to the exit.

00:07:39.450 --> 00:07:41.250
Ma'am, please come with me.

00:08:00.970 --> 00:08:01.970
This is a disaster.

00:08:03.370 --> 00:08:04.400
But how?

00:08:05.370 --> 00:08:07.140
What made her suspicious?

00:08:10.180 --> 00:08:13.450
What? After you said you visited the orphanage she abandoned you at?

00:08:14.250 --> 00:08:16.150
And even after you showed her the copy of her ID?

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:20.190
She gets caught red-handed and still makes excuses?

00:08:22.120 --> 00:08:24.320
How could that woman be my mother?

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:36.740
You said I should change the sign and make this my office, Mr. Lee.

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:42.780
Wow, isn't this a bit too grand for someone who's been sidelined?

00:08:43.480 --> 00:08:46.510
If someone as young as me were to occupy this symbolic office,

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:49.180
it would make me, the staff, and the executives uncomfortable.

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:52.420
Until I get a handle on the company and finish the first project,

00:08:52.490 --> 00:08:53.820
I'll be working out of the think tank.

00:08:54.220 --> 00:08:57.160
Besides, I can do approvals online, and we have video conferencing.

00:08:58.160 --> 00:09:02.260
For the antechamber, I've gathered some ideas like this.

00:09:05.470 --> 00:09:06.970
I can't really tell her not to work.

00:09:07.030 --> 00:09:08.330
Something along these lines.

00:09:12.470 --> 00:09:13.470
Come to my office.

00:09:19.910 --> 00:09:21.080
You can take a look.

00:09:25.520 --> 00:09:26.520
Yes.

00:09:33.690 --> 00:09:34.690
What did she say?

00:09:35.630 --> 00:09:37.430
I handled it.

00:09:39.130 --> 00:09:40.930
Sounds like she got the message.

00:09:42.470 --> 00:09:44.870
What about you? Are you okay?

00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:52.150
If that's all, may I go now?

00:09:52.850 --> 00:09:54.310
There's more I want to ask.

00:09:55.720 --> 00:09:56.720
It's just that you...

00:09:57.280 --> 00:09:58.580
look really exhausted.

00:10:00.050 --> 00:10:01.050
I am.

00:10:06.830 --> 00:10:08.060
(CEO's Office)

00:10:11.530 --> 00:10:13.300
She's unbelievable.

00:10:15.470 --> 00:10:17.140
Eun Oh's holding it together, though.

00:10:18.070 --> 00:10:22.040
She's holding up for now, probably fuelled by her anger and betrayal,

00:10:23.310 --> 00:10:25.810
but I'm worried about the emotional fallout later.

00:10:27.380 --> 00:10:28.650
Let's make sure we're there for her.

00:10:29.080 --> 00:10:30.480
It'll probably take some time, though.

00:10:32.950 --> 00:10:37.490
Since Eun Oh refused the transplant, I bet that woman is a total wreck.

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:51.240
I knew it smelled like November. That's snail extract, isn't it?

00:10:51.570 --> 00:10:54.110
Honey, you're home early.

00:10:54.670 --> 00:10:56.010
I'm home too.

00:10:56.710 --> 00:10:58.780
I ran into Dad out front.

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:01.650
Go wash up.

00:11:01.950 --> 00:11:03.519
It needs to simmer for ten more minutes.

00:11:03.520 --> 00:11:05.380
It'll be perfect when you're done.

00:11:06.150 --> 00:11:07.150
Okay, sounds good.

00:11:14.560 --> 00:11:15.830
Why are you staring at me like that?

00:11:18.230 --> 00:11:21.100
Because of the way you were looking at Mom.

00:11:22.600 --> 00:11:26.610
- Hey, you know I love your mother. - I know.

00:11:26.940 --> 00:11:27.940
I know, but...

00:11:30.180 --> 00:11:32.180
why do you love her?

00:11:33.150 --> 00:11:36.480
My gosh, Yeong Ra. What kind of question is that?

00:11:39.390 --> 00:11:40.990
Because she's always been so consistent.

00:11:43.690 --> 00:11:47.030
Even if she weren't like this, she'd still be a wonderful person.

00:11:47.490 --> 00:11:50.130
But no one stays this constant for 26 years.

00:11:51.460 --> 00:11:53.530
It's not easy for people to be like that.

00:11:55.400 --> 00:11:56.400
I see.

00:11:58.140 --> 00:12:00.870
You should learn from your mom and be just like her.

00:12:01.470 --> 00:12:04.440
Do that, and a man will be devoted for life.

00:12:07.150 --> 00:12:08.980
I'm not sure I can be like Mom, but...

00:12:09.850 --> 00:12:12.290
- Okay, Dad. - All right.

00:12:14.690 --> 00:12:18.360
She's so good to Dad. What is Mom up to?

00:12:20.030 --> 00:12:21.530
I'm dying of curiosity.

00:12:25.600 --> 00:12:26.800
You're not doing what?

00:12:27.500 --> 00:12:29.200
You're not doing the liver transplant?

00:12:29.900 --> 00:12:30.900
But why?

00:12:31.940 --> 00:12:33.470
Because I think you were right, Mom.

00:12:34.810 --> 00:12:36.310
I told her I'm not doing it.

00:12:37.280 --> 00:12:38.280
You did?

00:12:39.910 --> 00:12:43.780
And she just agreed to that? There's no way she would.

00:12:45.120 --> 00:12:47.050
If I say no, it means no.

00:12:48.990 --> 00:12:51.760
- Mom, the menu's out in two days. - What?

00:12:51.920 --> 00:12:53.160
How are the preparations coming along?

00:12:53.390 --> 00:12:55.160
Oh, right.

00:12:55.430 --> 00:12:57.400
We're putting up the banner tomorrow.

00:12:57.660 --> 00:13:02.100
We'll also update the kiosk, and Gang Oh will hand out flyers.

00:13:02.170 --> 00:13:05.100
I need to prep the menu text too. Gosh, it's so hectic.

00:13:05.440 --> 00:13:07.140
You should come check it out the evening after tomorrow.

00:13:07.970 --> 00:13:10.040
What am I, a customer? Just coming to "check it out?"

00:13:10.910 --> 00:13:12.280
I'll come by during your break.

00:13:14.750 --> 00:13:16.280
Just because Eun Oh refused...

00:13:16.680 --> 00:13:18.550
doesn't mean that woman will give up.

00:13:19.490 --> 00:13:21.520
- Listen, Eun Oh. - Mom.

00:13:22.320 --> 00:13:24.460
Mom, please just drop it. Okay?

00:13:26.990 --> 00:13:27.990
All right.

00:13:29.800 --> 00:13:31.200
I wonder what happened.

00:13:55.190 --> 00:13:56.390
Tell them not to break down the door.

00:13:56.990 --> 00:13:58.320
I'll leave once I'm done talking.

00:14:00.330 --> 00:14:01.890
- Eun Oh! - Ms. Ji?

00:14:14.170 --> 00:14:16.880
What company has so little respect for a team leader's privacy?

00:14:18.410 --> 00:14:20.080
Are you surprised to see me again?

00:14:21.380 --> 00:14:22.620
She's here to beg.

00:14:24.720 --> 00:14:25.990
I'm not here to beg.

00:14:30.320 --> 00:14:32.660
Is this the kind of person you are?

00:14:35.930 --> 00:14:37.830
I couldn't sleep a wink last night.

00:14:39.030 --> 00:14:41.930
How can you so cold-heartedly decide to let your own brother die?

00:14:42.670 --> 00:14:43.769
If you didn't know, it's one thing,

00:14:43.770 --> 00:14:46.170
but you know your twin brother needs a liver transplant.

00:14:46.410 --> 00:14:48.270
I believe I made myself perfectly clear yesterday.

00:14:49.040 --> 00:14:50.340
I don't have a twin brother.

00:14:51.180 --> 00:14:52.850
You're the one who abandoned me.

00:14:53.610 --> 00:14:55.450
And you made sure I could never be found.

00:14:55.880 --> 00:14:58.220
You left no record of my ID number or my parents' names.

00:14:59.120 --> 00:15:01.720
And after all that, you dare to act like we're family?

00:15:04.890 --> 00:15:06.190
Then that makes you a murderer.

00:15:09.030 --> 00:15:11.860
If your brother dies, you'll be a murderer.

00:15:13.400 --> 00:15:16.570
So don't make this about me. Think about your brother.

00:15:17.400 --> 00:15:20.270
Do you want your brother to die? It's me you want to hurt, isn't it?

00:15:20.610 --> 00:15:23.010
Then why hurt your innocent brother and not me?

00:15:25.110 --> 00:15:28.780
If you refuse this because of me, you'll be killing your brother.

00:15:33.050 --> 00:15:35.920
That's not an easy thing to live with.

00:15:37.020 --> 00:15:39.660
Will you be able to sleep at night after killing someone?

00:15:40.830 --> 00:15:44.100
Don't do something you'll regret just because you're angry with me.

00:15:46.400 --> 00:15:50.400
You've got it all backward. He wouldn't be dying because of me.

00:15:50.670 --> 00:15:53.810
- He'd be dying because of you. - No, it's because of you!

00:15:54.140 --> 00:15:56.040
Because it's your liver he needs.

00:15:57.640 --> 00:16:00.380
Are you okay with your brother dying because of you?

00:16:03.350 --> 00:16:04.350
Answer me.

00:16:06.920 --> 00:16:08.820
If he dies,

00:16:09.920 --> 00:16:12.320
it's because you're his mother. He's dying because of you.

00:16:14.060 --> 00:16:16.530
So you're really not going to do it?

00:16:19.130 --> 00:16:20.600
The surgery is in ten days.

00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:23.270
If you don't do this for him,

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:25.100
your brother is going to die.

00:16:26.370 --> 00:16:27.870
He is absolutely going to die.

00:16:31.580 --> 00:16:33.280
If you're done talking, you can leave.

00:16:56.740 --> 00:16:58.670
I guess it's time to tell them.

00:17:04.510 --> 00:17:05.580
Are you really going to be like this?

00:17:06.710 --> 00:17:08.510
Let's be rational about this, Eun Oh.

00:17:08.850 --> 00:17:10.480
I have been thinking about it rationally.

00:17:11.420 --> 00:17:12.490
Now, please leave.

00:17:13.450 --> 00:17:15.190
I'm not leaving until you give me an answer.

00:17:15.350 --> 00:17:18.260
If you were going to act like this, you shouldn't have gone so far.

00:17:18.860 --> 00:17:20.090
Telling me we'd live together...

00:17:21.130 --> 00:17:24.800
You shouldn't have told that lie about getting a divorce for me.

00:17:26.000 --> 00:17:27.800
In your pyjamas and barefoot.

00:17:28.530 --> 00:17:31.970
For someone so meticulous, I wonder why you weren't prepared.

00:17:34.970 --> 00:17:36.710
I didn't want to hurt you.

00:17:37.010 --> 00:17:39.450
I just wanted to save your brother without hurting you. That's all.

00:17:41.250 --> 00:17:44.450
If you had just begged me from the start, I would've done it.

00:17:48.450 --> 00:17:49.820
What a shame for that son of yours.

00:17:52.830 --> 00:17:54.190
Hey, Ji Eun Oh.

00:17:56.100 --> 00:17:57.130
Ji Eun Oh!

00:17:57.830 --> 00:17:59.730
Why is the door locked in the middle of work?

00:18:00.300 --> 00:18:01.330
Shouldn't you be working?

00:18:03.100 --> 00:18:04.100
Eun Oh.

00:18:12.080 --> 00:18:13.250
Did you lock this door?

00:18:13.980 --> 00:18:16.220
Get out, now. Before I throw you out myself.

00:18:30.130 --> 00:18:31.500
She threatened me.

00:18:32.460 --> 00:18:33.800
She even resorted to threats.

00:18:37.400 --> 00:18:41.040
(Woo Jin)

00:18:45.540 --> 00:18:46.550
Woo Jin.

00:18:47.850 --> 00:18:48.850
Ji Eun Oh.

00:18:49.280 --> 00:18:52.220
Hey, why did you call me on this?

00:18:52.790 --> 00:18:54.120
To save on the international calling fees.

00:18:59.330 --> 00:19:01.390
How have you been?

00:19:02.290 --> 00:19:03.300
What?

00:19:04.500 --> 00:19:05.830
Eun Oh, what's wrong? Your voice...

00:19:07.200 --> 00:19:08.600
Wait. Something's wrong, isn't it?

00:19:09.740 --> 00:19:10.740
Woo Jin.

00:19:12.740 --> 00:19:13.740
Woo Jin...

00:19:15.940 --> 00:19:17.180
The truth is...

00:19:18.640 --> 00:19:20.110
I was adopted.

00:19:21.980 --> 00:19:23.020
What did you say?

00:19:25.120 --> 00:19:26.950
I met my birth mother.

00:19:27.820 --> 00:19:32.290
But she was just pretending to be a client to get to me.

00:19:33.630 --> 00:19:35.390
Woo Jin, apparently, I'm a twin.

00:19:37.400 --> 00:19:40.030
And because my twin brother needs a liver transplant...

00:19:40.700 --> 00:19:42.640
That's why she came to me.

00:19:43.370 --> 00:19:44.700
A liver transplant?

00:19:45.240 --> 00:19:48.270
We "just happened" to meet, and she "just happened" to hire me.

00:19:49.680 --> 00:19:51.940
For months, she was so incredibly nice to me,

00:19:52.680 --> 00:19:54.080
and I really grew to like her.

00:19:55.910 --> 00:19:58.080
I really liked her.

00:20:00.250 --> 00:20:01.690
But all of it...

00:20:02.920 --> 00:20:06.690
It was all a ploy to soften me up and have me test for the transplant.

00:20:10.100 --> 00:20:11.730
Wait, you're a twin?

00:20:14.500 --> 00:20:18.970
Thinking about every single moment she was lying still drives me crazy.

00:20:20.240 --> 00:20:23.040
So manipulative and deceitful.

00:20:23.840 --> 00:20:25.410
And that's the woman who's supposed to be my mother.

00:20:27.250 --> 00:20:29.520
The woman who only wanted to take my liver...

00:20:30.550 --> 00:20:32.120
is the one who gave birth to me.

00:20:38.060 --> 00:20:40.260
- And so I... - I'm so sorry, Eun Oh.

00:20:41.390 --> 00:20:43.100
I just stepped out of class for a second.

00:20:43.760 --> 00:20:46.000
Don't cry, okay? I'll call you right back.

00:20:46.600 --> 00:20:48.530
Don't cry, all right?

00:20:53.510 --> 00:20:55.070
Han Woo Jin, what was that about?

00:21:02.080 --> 00:21:03.080
It can't be...

00:21:09.990 --> 00:21:12.990
(Team Leader's Office)

00:21:31.380 --> 00:21:34.480
Gosh, you have all this long hair, and you can't even style the back?

00:21:34.850 --> 00:21:37.880
My little sister does it in a flash. Her hands are a blur.

00:21:38.080 --> 00:21:40.120
The only thing I've ever used on my hair is a blow-dryer.

00:21:40.520 --> 00:21:43.120
- I get this done at a salon. - A salon?

00:21:44.190 --> 00:21:46.760
Right. You're a third-generation heiress.

00:21:47.560 --> 00:21:48.630
It slipped my mind.

00:21:54.030 --> 00:21:55.130
All done?

00:22:19.220 --> 00:22:20.990
Yeong Ra, you look really...

00:22:23.430 --> 00:22:26.930
I mean, you look like a real writer.

00:22:29.570 --> 00:22:31.070
(Director Ko)

00:22:31.170 --> 00:22:36.040
Hey, Director Ko is on the move. From Pyeongja-dong, heading north.

00:22:36.580 --> 00:22:38.240
That's toward the hospital.

00:22:39.240 --> 00:22:40.650
Let's go. Quick.

00:22:42.250 --> 00:22:43.320
Got the gear?

00:22:53.690 --> 00:22:55.390
(Cheong Ah University Hospital, Lee Ji Soo, Kim Jae Yeong)

00:22:57.060 --> 00:22:59.060
We agreed to start on the top floor and work our way down, right?

00:22:59.870 --> 00:23:02.200
That way, we can check everywhere without missing anything.

00:23:31.960 --> 00:23:33.470
A liver for you...

00:23:34.230 --> 00:23:35.500
I've secured one.

00:23:37.200 --> 00:23:38.200
What?

00:23:39.540 --> 00:23:42.410
How? I'm still way down the list.

00:23:42.510 --> 00:23:43.740
You don't need to know how.

00:23:53.320 --> 00:23:55.450
You should be resting. Why are you up and about?

00:23:57.960 --> 00:23:59.830
You didn't say you were coming to the hospital.

00:24:01.090 --> 00:24:02.530
Did something happen?

00:24:03.430 --> 00:24:05.660
No. I just felt like I had to see you.

00:24:07.730 --> 00:24:08.730
Well...

00:24:09.670 --> 00:24:12.440
How did you find a donor for my surgery?

00:24:13.770 --> 00:24:16.040
I told you. You don't need to know that.

00:24:16.680 --> 00:24:18.280
All you need to know is it wasn't easy.

00:24:20.910 --> 00:24:23.420
That donor you had such a hard time finding...

00:24:26.420 --> 00:24:28.050
Is her name Ji Eun Oh, by any chance?

00:24:35.060 --> 00:24:36.160
What are you talking about?

00:24:39.900 --> 00:24:41.370
So, it's true.

00:24:42.570 --> 00:24:46.240
The liver is from the very person you abandoned so cruelly?

00:24:46.310 --> 00:24:48.140
From my little sister?

00:24:49.310 --> 00:24:50.310
What?

00:24:50.610 --> 00:24:53.510
That's confidential information. Who told you?

00:24:53.580 --> 00:24:55.310
- Who blabbed? - Mom!

00:24:55.480 --> 00:24:57.150
You tell me how you found out first!

00:24:59.990 --> 00:25:01.590
No, you tell me first.

00:25:05.090 --> 00:25:06.660
You told me she was dead.

00:25:07.830 --> 00:25:10.200
You told me Yu Ra was dead!

00:25:11.130 --> 00:25:13.000
And now, after all this time, you found her?

00:25:14.000 --> 00:25:15.530
Did you trick her again?

00:25:17.570 --> 00:25:20.270
How could you?

00:25:20.340 --> 00:25:22.440
Where does it end with you, Mom?

00:25:25.310 --> 00:25:26.350
And you...

00:25:27.510 --> 00:25:30.180
You never forgot about her? Even after I told you she was dead?

00:25:32.150 --> 00:25:33.750
How could I forget?

00:25:35.250 --> 00:25:39.160
I left Yu Ra there all alone and just followed you.

00:25:39.220 --> 00:25:40.330
Let's go.

00:25:40.860 --> 00:25:42.590
Yu Ra.

00:25:42.890 --> 00:25:44.900
Brother!

00:25:45.630 --> 00:25:49.400
- Yu Ra! - Mom!

00:25:49.470 --> 00:25:51.900
Yu Ra!

00:25:54.110 --> 00:25:55.810
You remembered that?

00:25:57.040 --> 00:25:59.210
You never said a word to me about it.

00:26:00.710 --> 00:26:02.910
Because you told me never to bring it up again.

00:26:03.550 --> 00:26:05.950
Because I knew what would happen if I did.

00:26:09.520 --> 00:26:11.520
To think you remembered something so useless.

00:26:21.800 --> 00:26:23.170
I'm not getting the liver transplant.

00:26:24.700 --> 00:26:28.510
No one sane throws their life away when there's a chance to live.

00:26:28.810 --> 00:26:31.580
- People die when they lose hope. - No.

00:26:33.610 --> 00:26:35.180
I won't take Yu Ra's liver.

00:26:40.050 --> 00:26:43.520
That is not your decision to make.

00:27:33.070 --> 00:27:34.440
Excuse me, doctors. What floor?

00:27:37.880 --> 00:27:38.980
Hello? Doctors?

00:27:40.480 --> 00:27:41.610
You haven't selected a floor.

00:27:44.380 --> 00:27:45.780
- Dr. Lee. - Yes?

00:27:46.320 --> 00:27:48.150
Why didn't you press the button?

00:27:49.720 --> 00:27:51.290
I thought you pressed it.

00:27:57.730 --> 00:28:00.070
Hey, these are all private rooms.

00:28:00.500 --> 00:28:02.700
So, Mom's boyfriend is in a private room?

00:28:02.930 --> 00:28:05.670
We're looking for a guy in his 50s, right?

00:28:06.140 --> 00:28:07.140
No.

00:28:07.410 --> 00:28:10.080
My mom's pretty. She could have a younger boyfriend.

00:28:10.440 --> 00:28:12.480
All right, down to early 40s, then.

00:28:15.510 --> 00:28:18.180
Okay, skip this one. It's an old man.

00:28:28.390 --> 00:28:29.530
I wonder who put this up.

00:28:31.130 --> 00:28:32.200
She's gone.

00:28:33.300 --> 00:28:34.430
Check the room next door, too.

00:28:34.900 --> 00:28:35.900
Okay.

00:28:37.300 --> 00:28:39.100
Hey, no. This guy's in his 20s.

00:28:39.770 --> 00:28:41.010
Definitely not a guy in his 20s.

00:28:43.140 --> 00:28:44.140
What?

00:28:44.510 --> 00:28:45.610
Han Woo Jin?

00:28:46.340 --> 00:28:47.410
What? What's wrong?

00:28:48.410 --> 00:28:50.220
He has the same name as my brother.

00:28:50.420 --> 00:28:51.420
(Han Woo Jin, M)

00:29:03.300 --> 00:29:05.930
It's my brother... Woo Jin.

00:29:07.000 --> 00:29:08.170
It's really him. My second-oldest brother.

00:29:08.600 --> 00:29:09.600
Your second-oldest brother?

00:29:10.300 --> 00:29:12.470
I thought you said he was studying in the US.

00:29:13.040 --> 00:29:14.040
Yes.

00:29:15.770 --> 00:29:17.210
Why is he in the hospital?

00:29:19.140 --> 00:29:23.280
- Because he's sick, obviously. - With what?

00:29:24.680 --> 00:29:26.820
And why would my mom try to hide this?

00:29:28.590 --> 00:29:30.590
Hey, let's just ask the nurse.

00:29:31.860 --> 00:29:34.859
Hey. We're in disguise, remember?

00:29:34.860 --> 00:29:38.029
Look, residents rotate every month,

00:29:38.030 --> 00:29:39.760
so the nurses may not know all of them.

00:29:41.600 --> 00:29:43.240
- Really? - Yes.

00:29:47.570 --> 00:29:51.310
Hi, I just need to confirm the professor's orders.

00:29:51.410 --> 00:29:53.750
Could I get the chart for Han Woo Jin, please?

00:29:54.950 --> 00:29:57.350
- The patient, Han Woo Jin? - Yes.

00:30:02.350 --> 00:30:03.490
Nurse Im!

00:30:03.860 --> 00:30:05.060
Did you change your cushion foundation?

00:30:06.630 --> 00:30:08.560
Your makeup looks amazing today.

00:30:09.860 --> 00:30:11.160
Really?

00:30:11.760 --> 00:30:14.870
If you tried an orange lip tint, it'd look even better.

00:30:15.530 --> 00:30:18.440
- I've never tried an orange shade. - Really?

00:30:18.500 --> 00:30:19.740
I actually have a cool undertone.

00:30:19.800 --> 00:30:22.570
You really look amazing, but could we please see the chart?

00:30:23.210 --> 00:30:25.910
Right. When I had my colours done, they said my lips were too blue,

00:30:25.980 --> 00:30:27.480
so they actually did tell me to wear orange.

00:30:27.550 --> 00:30:30.920
So what cushion did you switch to? Your skin looks incredible.

00:30:31.820 --> 00:30:35.520
- But your skin is even better. - Gosh, stop.

00:30:36.820 --> 00:30:37.820
(Han Woo Jin, end-stage liver disease)

00:30:37.890 --> 00:30:38.890
(Planned for liver transplant)

00:30:44.660 --> 00:30:45.660
Thanks so much!

00:30:46.030 --> 00:30:47.530
I wasn't done reading that.

00:30:47.770 --> 00:30:48.930
Sorry, we're busy. We have to get going.

00:30:49.470 --> 00:30:50.799
Hey, what was that about?

00:30:50.800 --> 00:30:52.770
It was all in English. I'd only just started memorizing it.

00:30:53.740 --> 00:30:54.810
He needs a liver transplant.

00:30:55.440 --> 00:30:56.440
A liver transplant?

00:31:01.650 --> 00:31:04.180
So that's what's going on.

00:31:06.280 --> 00:31:10.220
But still, why would his illness be a weakness?

00:31:10.960 --> 00:31:14.590
- Does your father hate Woo Jin? - No, that's not it.

00:31:16.130 --> 00:31:17.130
This is just...

00:31:18.660 --> 00:31:19.930
all part of my mom's plan.

00:31:21.400 --> 00:31:23.230
Living in your father's shadow isn't enough.

00:31:23.840 --> 00:31:25.499
You need to have your own accomplishments.

00:31:25.500 --> 00:31:28.770
That's how you reach a higher level in this world.

00:31:28.840 --> 00:31:33.040
That's why I'm pushing you up there, no matter what it takes.

00:31:34.280 --> 00:31:35.850
This world is all about social class,

00:31:37.050 --> 00:31:39.750
and because of that, we get looked down on.

00:31:42.190 --> 00:31:43.190
Yeong Ra.

00:31:44.990 --> 00:31:45.990
Ji Wan.

00:31:46.860 --> 00:31:48.930
I'm suddenly not so sure anymore.

00:31:50.560 --> 00:31:51.700
I'm not sure I can defy my mom.

00:31:56.330 --> 00:31:58.170
My mom will never give up on me.

00:32:16.290 --> 00:32:17.620
What kind of mother does that?

00:32:18.460 --> 00:32:20.130
My mom would never do that.

00:32:20.930 --> 00:32:23.660
Neither would my dad, my grandma, my brother, or Su Bin.

00:32:25.400 --> 00:32:26.400
Park Yeong Ra.

00:32:27.000 --> 00:32:29.030
What kind of world did you grow up in?

00:32:29.470 --> 00:32:30.470
You poor thing.

00:32:42.950 --> 00:32:44.180
It smells so warm in here.

00:32:45.520 --> 00:32:47.220
So cosy. This is home.

00:32:51.590 --> 00:32:54.630
Why is Ji Wan just standing there like that?

00:32:58.530 --> 00:33:00.700
- Hey. Hush! - Grandma.

00:33:02.430 --> 00:33:03.440
Come on.

00:33:03.900 --> 00:33:05.000
Why?

00:33:14.680 --> 00:33:15.680
Hurry up and spit it out.

00:33:16.410 --> 00:33:19.820
You're in money trouble, aren't you? How much? Is it bad?

00:33:20.090 --> 00:33:21.650
No, Grandma.

00:33:22.350 --> 00:33:25.420
You could've just gone to your room. Why were you standing there...

00:33:25.490 --> 00:33:29.290
like you'd seen a ghost, staring at your parents' room?

00:33:29.690 --> 00:33:31.030
No, it's just that...

00:33:32.560 --> 00:33:34.830
It's just hard to explain.

00:33:37.170 --> 00:33:38.170
Listen.

00:33:38.840 --> 00:33:39.840
I...

00:33:40.940 --> 00:33:42.310
I can give you a thousand dollars.

00:33:42.910 --> 00:33:44.080
That's my entire life savings.

00:33:44.510 --> 00:33:46.580
I told you. It's not about money.

00:33:47.910 --> 00:33:50.380
But Grandma, how do you have a thousand dollars?

00:33:50.480 --> 00:33:52.850
I saved it up, little by little.

00:33:54.520 --> 00:33:57.760
Why? Is that not enough?

00:33:58.190 --> 00:33:59.190
How much do you need?

00:34:00.130 --> 00:34:01.460
That's her entire life savings,

00:34:01.960 --> 00:34:03.260
and she'd give it all to me?

00:34:04.500 --> 00:34:05.500
Grandma...

00:34:05.800 --> 00:34:07.730
Goodness, hey. What's gotten into you?

00:34:09.300 --> 00:34:12.670
I'm just so glad I was born into this family,

00:34:14.040 --> 00:34:15.610
and I'm so grateful for you, Grandma.

00:34:17.180 --> 00:34:18.180
For goodness' sake.

00:34:18.840 --> 00:34:20.410
What's all this nonsense out of the blue?

00:34:22.810 --> 00:34:23.950
Listen, Ji Wan.

00:34:25.580 --> 00:34:28.350
Are you absolutely sure nothing's wrong?

00:34:28.690 --> 00:34:31.820
Yes, I'm sure. Nothing's wrong. I promise, Grandma.

00:34:33.060 --> 00:34:34.060
And...

00:34:35.130 --> 00:34:36.130
thank you.

00:34:46.340 --> 00:34:48.370
Grandma, you're a natural for a beginner!

00:34:52.710 --> 00:34:54.650
Grandma, why don't you take a short break?

00:34:57.080 --> 00:34:58.080
Are you home?

00:34:58.480 --> 00:34:59.850
Let's get something good to eat after I get off work.

00:35:01.090 --> 00:35:03.820
I'll pick you up when I'm done, so stay home.

00:35:07.730 --> 00:35:08.730
Don't come here.

00:35:08.731 --> 00:35:10.800
Text me the location, and I'll meet you there.

00:35:11.430 --> 00:35:14.030
What if someone sees you in my neighbourhood?

00:35:15.030 --> 00:35:16.900
If anyone asks, I'll just say I came to see Ji Hyuk.

00:35:18.140 --> 00:35:22.010
You said Ji Hyuk can't find out. Funny how he's your best alibi now.

00:35:25.180 --> 00:35:26.180
Let me take another one.

00:35:29.280 --> 00:35:31.680
When Woo Jin suddenly came home the other day,

00:35:33.020 --> 00:35:34.690
was he trying to tell us something?

00:35:37.490 --> 00:35:38.490
Yeong Ra.

00:35:38.890 --> 00:35:40.690
No matter how much I think about it,

00:35:41.390 --> 00:35:44.630
I really think you should be the one to tell Chairman Park.

00:35:46.430 --> 00:35:48.070
I can't tell Dad.

00:35:48.530 --> 00:35:52.470
But didn't you say your mom's always on eggshells around your dad?

00:35:52.700 --> 00:35:54.410
Exactly. That's why I can't tell him.

00:35:54.670 --> 00:35:57.040
My mom hid it. You want me to go tattle on her to my dad?

00:35:57.610 --> 00:35:59.510
How am I supposed to deal with the fallout from that?

00:35:59.780 --> 00:36:01.180
Well, then...

00:36:01.880 --> 00:36:03.350
You should at least go visit him.

00:36:03.820 --> 00:36:06.780
Look, there's nothing worse than being sick and all alone.

00:36:08.350 --> 00:36:12.090
- What if I go and Mom finds out? - Wear a disguise again.

00:36:12.420 --> 00:36:13.960
Don't you feel bad for your brother at all?

00:36:15.190 --> 00:36:17.060
I do. I feel awful.

00:36:17.530 --> 00:36:19.600
But what if I'm there in disguise and my mom shows up?

00:36:19.930 --> 00:36:20.930
You think I wouldn't get caught?

00:36:22.100 --> 00:36:25.640
It's easy for you to talk since it's not your problem.

00:36:27.210 --> 00:36:30.440
That's not it. I'm not trying to be dismissive.

00:36:31.180 --> 00:36:33.879
It's just... Ignorance is one thing.

00:36:33.880 --> 00:36:35.380
But to know and just ignore him...

00:36:35.950 --> 00:36:39.150
Come on, that's just wrong.

00:36:39.580 --> 00:36:41.690
Don't judge my situation by your standards.

00:36:42.620 --> 00:36:45.260
They say there are things in the world that defy normal logic.

00:36:45.420 --> 00:36:47.930
Who said that? Your mom?

00:36:52.730 --> 00:36:54.930
What did I just say?

00:36:59.140 --> 00:37:01.310
I don't remember.

00:37:04.210 --> 00:37:05.880
You've already got so much on your mind,

00:37:06.610 --> 00:37:08.810
and I was just pushing my own opinion on you,

00:37:09.080 --> 00:37:10.080
Yeong Ra.

00:37:10.680 --> 00:37:12.720
Why don't you lie down on the sofa and rest?

00:37:13.520 --> 00:37:14.790
I'm going to go do my rounds.

00:37:30.340 --> 00:37:31.340
I'm sorry.

00:37:32.270 --> 00:37:33.270
It's okay.

00:37:33.770 --> 00:37:34.840
Call me if you need anything.

00:37:40.980 --> 00:37:42.979
(Damga Charcoal Grill)

00:37:42.980 --> 00:37:45.220
- Hi, welcome. How many? - We're meeting someone.

00:37:45.280 --> 00:37:47.120
- Right this way. - Hello. Welcome.

00:37:47.190 --> 00:37:49.519
- Hi, how many in your party? - Three of us.

00:37:49.520 --> 00:37:50.619
We'll clear a table and seat you shortly.

00:37:50.620 --> 00:37:51.660
- Sure. - Please wait just a moment.

00:37:52.160 --> 00:37:53.160
Unbelievable.

00:37:53.830 --> 00:37:55.360
Living in some cheap rental...

00:37:55.730 --> 00:37:58.659
And he's working at the restaurant she busted her back to open...

00:37:58.660 --> 00:37:59.660
for the family?

00:38:00.670 --> 00:38:02.300
(Damga Charcoal Grill)

00:38:02.370 --> 00:38:04.740
Here's the new meat dish you ordered.

00:38:06.440 --> 00:38:09.870
So, what do you think? Are you enjoying it?

00:38:11.610 --> 00:38:14.850
- It looks amazing and just melts. - Really?

00:38:15.710 --> 00:38:17.580
Thank you. Enjoy your meal.

00:38:22.350 --> 00:38:24.590
What? You're home already?

00:38:25.490 --> 00:38:27.260
Hold on. I'll get dinner ready for you right away.

00:38:27.330 --> 00:38:29.190
No, that's okay. I'm not eating dinner at home.

00:38:29.530 --> 00:38:30.560
I actually have to head out now.

00:38:31.860 --> 00:38:33.970
Why the black suit? Are you going to a funeral?

00:38:36.270 --> 00:38:37.940
Byeong Ho passed away.

00:38:38.800 --> 00:38:39.800
Byeong Ho?

00:38:40.540 --> 00:38:42.010
Your friend, Byeong Ho, in Mexico?

00:38:42.640 --> 00:38:44.110
The one who was great at guitar and singing?

00:38:44.980 --> 00:38:48.810
Yes. We're holding a small memorial for him at Yeong Bo's restaurant.

00:38:49.550 --> 00:38:51.750
My gosh, what happened? He was so healthy.

00:38:53.350 --> 00:38:54.350
Car accident.

00:38:54.950 --> 00:38:55.950
Oh, my gosh.

00:38:56.390 --> 00:38:58.020
But didn't he say he'd come back next year?

00:38:59.220 --> 00:39:02.790
He kept saying he was coming back for the past couple of years,

00:39:03.130 --> 00:39:06.060
but there was always something else. Factory machines, delivery issues...

00:39:06.700 --> 00:39:08.800
He promised he'd be here for sure on March 5 next year.

00:39:09.100 --> 00:39:12.270
He even sent a picture of his plane ticket reservation.

00:39:14.040 --> 00:39:15.210
That fool...

00:39:17.510 --> 00:39:20.310
Honey. You must be so heartbroken.

00:39:21.210 --> 00:39:23.880
Life just feels so pointless.

00:39:25.980 --> 00:39:27.120
I'll be back later.

00:39:30.560 --> 00:39:33.390
Can you believe we're all over 60,

00:39:33.860 --> 00:39:36.190
and this is the only picture we have of the five of us?

00:39:37.830 --> 00:39:39.130
Tell me about it.

00:39:41.070 --> 00:39:42.370
That darn Byeong Ho...

00:39:42.870 --> 00:39:45.400
Was he 35 when he moved to Mexico?

00:39:46.200 --> 00:39:47.970
We only saw him three times since, didn't we?

00:39:48.610 --> 00:39:50.740
Once was at my father's funeral.

00:39:51.910 --> 00:39:53.980
He went halfway across the world to make a living.

00:39:54.880 --> 00:39:56.850
His funeral must feel so lonely.

00:39:58.050 --> 00:40:00.990
Poor Byeong Ho must be heartbroken and lonely in his casket.

00:40:01.350 --> 00:40:03.490
The dead don't feel a thing. He's fine.

00:40:04.520 --> 00:40:06.190
It's harder on those of us left behind.

00:40:06.520 --> 00:40:07.530
That fool...

00:40:08.190 --> 00:40:09.730
I always felt so sorry for him.

00:40:10.900 --> 00:40:12.160
Man, back in college,

00:40:12.460 --> 00:40:15.600
the five of us were thick as thieves.

00:40:18.600 --> 00:40:20.710
Hey, how about a song?

00:40:21.940 --> 00:40:24.410
Byeong Ho left this when he moved, remember?

00:40:24.680 --> 00:40:26.209
He wanted us to get together and sing often.

00:40:26.210 --> 00:40:27.710
- Hey, Sang Cheol. - Yes?

00:40:28.710 --> 00:40:32.680
I haven't touched one in 30 years. Think I can still do it? My gosh.

00:40:33.150 --> 00:40:38.220
- I call out to the yonder sky - I call out to the yonder sky

00:40:38.290 --> 00:40:40.220
One, two, three, four!

00:40:40.490 --> 00:40:44.199
- Fly high into the sky - Fly high into the sky

00:40:44.200 --> 00:40:48.000
- Let my heart soar too - Let my heart soar too

00:40:48.600 --> 00:40:52.940
- Soar with my beautiful dreams - Soar with my beautiful dreams

00:41:05.450 --> 00:41:06.750
I can start contributing to the household expenses.

00:41:10.420 --> 00:41:13.720
I'm the head of this household. I'm the head of this family.

00:41:13.990 --> 00:41:17.700
How dare you sneak in here uninvited and act like you own the place?

00:41:17.830 --> 00:41:19.860
When I'm still alive and kicking!

00:41:21.330 --> 00:41:22.470
My goodness...

00:41:22.970 --> 00:41:24.270
Have a good day!

00:41:29.270 --> 00:41:30.270
I'm home.

00:41:30.340 --> 00:41:34.610
Oh, my! Look who's home. Our very own CEO!

00:41:35.180 --> 00:41:37.450
Yes, Grandma. Your CEO is home.

00:41:37.950 --> 00:41:38.950
Ji Hyuk, you must be exhausted.

00:41:39.280 --> 00:41:41.490
How in the world do you run a company?

00:41:42.020 --> 00:41:44.190
Ji Hyuk, have you eaten dinner yet?

00:41:44.590 --> 00:41:46.360
- I already ate. - I see.

00:41:46.390 --> 00:41:48.360
Then have some fruit. I'll bring some up for you.

00:41:49.030 --> 00:41:50.030
What kind of fruit?

00:41:50.160 --> 00:41:53.200
I got it at the market for Ji Hyuk, the rock of our family.

00:41:53.830 --> 00:41:57.670
No, I'm fine. You and Grandma can go ahead and have it.

00:41:58.570 --> 00:42:00.710
- I'm heading up. - Okay.

00:42:08.910 --> 00:42:11.880
Why are you watching him go upstairs too?

00:42:12.120 --> 00:42:13.120
Like he's some kind of king.

00:42:13.680 --> 00:42:16.520
You know, I find I can't treat him the way I used to, either.

00:42:17.220 --> 00:42:18.320
Is it because he's so successful now?

00:42:31.900 --> 00:42:33.100
Oh, come in.

00:42:36.870 --> 00:42:37.880
Here, have some of this.

00:42:38.940 --> 00:42:41.150
I noticed you stayed up past 1am after getting home last night.

00:42:42.380 --> 00:42:43.380
Thanks, Mom.

00:42:45.450 --> 00:42:47.290
Are you working on something urgent?

00:42:48.390 --> 00:42:49.550
Not really. Why do you ask?

00:42:51.220 --> 00:42:52.820
This will only take five minutes.

00:42:54.060 --> 00:42:56.790
Why? Is there some kind of family emergency?

00:42:57.630 --> 00:42:58.630
No.

00:42:59.760 --> 00:43:02.800
Ji Hyuk, how about you get your own place?

00:43:03.100 --> 00:43:04.100
Somewhere near your office.

00:43:05.370 --> 00:43:06.370
Get my own place?

00:43:07.340 --> 00:43:11.240
You sleep at the office so often. Isn't your commute exhausting?

00:43:12.380 --> 00:43:16.350
You can afford a studio near work, can't you? You're the CEO.

00:43:17.280 --> 00:43:18.350
That's not the point.

00:43:19.150 --> 00:43:21.350
Mom, why are you suddenly kicking me out?

00:43:23.750 --> 00:43:26.390
I hate seeing your father walk on eggshells around you.

00:43:27.960 --> 00:43:29.590
You think Dad walks on eggshells around me?

00:43:30.030 --> 00:43:31.160
No, Mom.

00:43:31.900 --> 00:43:34.130
He's just sulking because he disapproves of me.

00:43:35.100 --> 00:43:36.100
Right.

00:43:36.400 --> 00:43:37.940
As if a child could ever understand their parents.

00:43:39.700 --> 00:43:40.940
That's part of it, but...

00:43:41.810 --> 00:43:44.840
Now that I'm working, it's too much to take care of everyone at home.

00:43:45.710 --> 00:43:47.210
And ever since you became the CEO,

00:43:47.950 --> 00:43:50.720
you've been making me nervous. It's hard to be around you.

00:43:53.480 --> 00:43:54.490
Mom.

00:43:55.050 --> 00:43:56.250
Gosh, I don't know.

00:43:56.850 --> 00:43:59.220
I know it sounds petty, but I can't help it.

00:44:00.460 --> 00:44:02.560
So, let's just make life easier for everyone.

00:44:03.460 --> 00:44:05.130
Honestly, it's time for you to move out.

00:44:10.400 --> 00:44:12.240
Okay. I'll start looking for a place.

00:44:14.840 --> 00:44:16.310
Here's the beer you ordered.

00:44:16.470 --> 00:44:20.180
- Why so long? Did you make it? - I'm sorry.

00:44:21.980 --> 00:44:23.780
And we asked for more of this side dish.

00:44:24.320 --> 00:44:26.420
Oh, I must not have heard you earlier.

00:44:26.820 --> 00:44:28.590
- I'll get that for you. - Hey.

00:44:28.750 --> 00:44:29.750
Yes?

00:44:30.620 --> 00:44:33.190
You're supposed to say, "I'm sorry" first.

00:44:33.990 --> 00:44:36.190
But earlier, you only asked for two beers.

00:44:37.500 --> 00:44:40.500
We all heard him ask for more side dishes,

00:44:41.000 --> 00:44:42.930
and you're the only one who didn't. Are you trying to argue?

00:44:43.930 --> 00:44:47.269
- Okay, I'll get it. - I told you to apologise!

00:44:47.270 --> 00:44:48.410
Hey, come on!

00:44:48.940 --> 00:44:50.470
Just leave it. Let him be.

00:44:50.910 --> 00:44:52.640
He's going to be waiting tables his whole life anyway.

00:44:56.410 --> 00:44:59.480
I'm not just waiting tables here. I'm the owner's son.

00:45:01.320 --> 00:45:04.990
So what, does that make you the owner? I'm so jealous.

00:45:05.390 --> 00:45:07.490
You've got no prospects and no skills,

00:45:07.890 --> 00:45:10.230
but at least you're lucky your folks let you wait tables here.

00:45:12.300 --> 00:45:15.130
Gang Oh, what are you doing? The additional meat order is up.

00:45:16.930 --> 00:45:17.940
Unbelievable.

00:45:19.070 --> 00:45:21.110
Gang Oh, check the charcoal grill. Something seems off.

00:45:21.170 --> 00:45:22.710
And has the meat for table two gone out yet?

00:45:22.770 --> 00:45:23.770
It needs to go out right away.

00:45:24.580 --> 00:45:26.910
Why does everyone keep ordering me around?

00:45:27.240 --> 00:45:28.250
Ji Gang Oh!

00:45:29.950 --> 00:45:31.550
Hey! Where's that side dish?

00:45:51.840 --> 00:45:55.110
- Mom. You worked so hard today. - Yes.

00:45:55.170 --> 00:45:58.080
Mom, the new menu's a smash hit. The response was amazing.

00:45:58.480 --> 00:46:01.410
It's completely different from just cooking it for you kids.

00:46:01.650 --> 00:46:05.980
When customers say it's delicious, it makes me so proud, you know?

00:46:06.050 --> 00:46:07.520
- Really? - Of course.

00:46:07.590 --> 00:46:09.650
- It was a great idea, wasn't it? - Yes.

00:46:10.620 --> 00:46:14.690
Oh, my goodness. Eun Oh, look at your dark circles.

00:46:14.860 --> 00:46:17.530
- You go on home ahead of me. - No, I'll go home with you.

00:46:17.600 --> 00:46:20.900
Come on, not much left to clean. Plus, you have work tomorrow.

00:46:21.170 --> 00:46:23.729
Mom, your eyes are bloodshot too.

00:46:23.730 --> 00:46:25.140
- What? - You must be exhausted from today.

00:46:28.640 --> 00:46:31.510
Gang Oh. Listen, for tonight,

00:46:31.740 --> 00:46:34.350
your sister and I will head home a little early.

00:46:34.880 --> 00:46:36.350
Could you finish closing up here?

00:46:37.580 --> 00:46:39.880
Sure. Don't worry, I got it.

00:46:40.120 --> 00:46:43.690
- We appreciate it, Ji Gang Oh. - Thanks, honey.

00:46:43.750 --> 00:46:45.120
- Mom, go get changed. - Okay.

00:46:49.690 --> 00:46:53.000
(Damga Charcoal Grill)

00:47:04.170 --> 00:47:05.980
And I get no appreciation for all my hard work.

00:47:07.080 --> 00:47:08.850
Getting disrespected by customers... Darn it.

00:47:09.810 --> 00:47:10.920
And I'm the one who worked the hardest.

00:47:28.070 --> 00:47:29.370
I'm your sister's mother.

00:47:30.330 --> 00:47:31.340
Her birth mother.

00:47:32.340 --> 00:47:33.340
What?

00:47:36.640 --> 00:47:37.940
Hey, where are you going?

00:47:38.580 --> 00:47:39.810
So, what's this about?

00:47:40.910 --> 00:47:42.350
Let's sit down and talk.

00:47:44.050 --> 00:47:45.050
Please, sit.

00:47:46.750 --> 00:47:48.720
I don't see why I should have to. Darn it.

00:47:54.690 --> 00:47:56.030
I'm sure your sister told you.

00:47:56.760 --> 00:47:58.500
And you must be very angry with me.

00:47:59.030 --> 00:48:00.730
Just get to the point, please.

00:48:04.270 --> 00:48:08.210
Giving someone a piece of your liver is no small thing.

00:48:08.910 --> 00:48:09.910
It's scary, too.

00:48:10.410 --> 00:48:11.880
So what's your point?

00:48:13.540 --> 00:48:14.650
Your sister...

00:48:16.450 --> 00:48:17.550
Could you convince her?

00:48:22.450 --> 00:48:23.450
It's 500,000 dollars.

00:48:25.020 --> 00:48:26.020
What?

00:48:30.090 --> 00:48:31.830
Now that the surgery date is getting closer,

00:48:32.300 --> 00:48:34.400
I think your sister is getting cold feet.

00:48:35.730 --> 00:48:38.070
I'll give you another 500,000 when the surgery is over.

00:48:45.810 --> 00:48:47.010
To you, Gang Oh,

00:48:47.610 --> 00:48:49.280
I must seem terribly shameless, right?

00:48:51.550 --> 00:48:54.950
Well, yes, kind of.

00:48:57.890 --> 00:49:01.930
But your sister and my son... They're twins.

00:49:03.990 --> 00:49:07.100
So what was I supposed to do?

00:49:08.470 --> 00:49:09.970
When I had to weigh the guilt I feel for my daughter...

00:49:11.140 --> 00:49:13.300
against the life of my dying son,

00:49:15.270 --> 00:49:18.840
what kind of mother was I supposed to be?

00:49:21.050 --> 00:49:22.810
Why are you asking me that?

00:49:26.580 --> 00:49:29.050
Your sister won't forgive herself if her own flesh and blood dies.

00:49:30.820 --> 00:49:33.620
Don't mention we met.

00:49:34.590 --> 00:49:37.390
Just tell her this liver transplant is about saving a life.

00:49:38.930 --> 00:49:40.560
That's all you need to say to your sister.

00:49:42.100 --> 00:49:43.670
You're offering a million dollars just to say something to her?

00:49:45.340 --> 00:49:47.069
I meant to give it to your mother...

00:49:47.070 --> 00:49:48.710
to thank her for raising my daughter.

00:49:51.210 --> 00:49:53.610
I'm too embarrassed to give it to her, so I'm giving it to you.

00:49:59.320 --> 00:50:02.120
You'll get the rest when the surgery is over.

00:50:06.520 --> 00:50:08.290
Wait, this...

00:50:27.380 --> 00:50:29.680
She's right. There's a price for raising someone.

00:50:30.350 --> 00:50:31.520
What should I do with all this?

00:50:32.250 --> 00:50:34.890
That's right. First, we'll get a three-bedroom apartment.

00:50:34.950 --> 00:50:37.720
Eun Oh needs her own room. How long can she share with Mom?

00:50:38.790 --> 00:50:40.560
But, man, that woman is so naive.

00:50:41.790 --> 00:50:44.090
She doesn't know our Ji Eun Oh at all.

00:50:45.700 --> 00:50:48.200
My sister might be hesitating, but there's no way she'd back out.

00:50:49.330 --> 00:50:51.800
She doesn't know her own daughter because she didn't raise her.

00:50:53.140 --> 00:50:55.240
Ji Eun Oh is Mom's daughter.

00:50:56.810 --> 00:50:58.810
(Vice President Park Seong Jae)

00:51:06.020 --> 00:51:08.550
Seong Jae, I'm in the lobby.

00:51:08.890 --> 00:51:10.220
Can you come down and get me?

00:51:10.890 --> 00:51:11.890
The lobby?

00:51:17.130 --> 00:51:19.100
(Shoealls)

00:51:19.160 --> 00:51:21.100
I told you to stop doing this.

00:51:21.700 --> 00:51:24.700
- Why did you bring me food again? - I didn't make it.

00:51:25.440 --> 00:51:28.310
My mom made spicy stir-fried octopus and beef for dinner,

00:51:28.840 --> 00:51:30.140
and it was so good,

00:51:30.740 --> 00:51:31.910
I snuck some for you.

00:51:33.010 --> 00:51:35.650
I remembered how much you seemed to enjoy it last time.

00:51:41.690 --> 00:51:44.090
That... You remembered that?

00:51:44.690 --> 00:51:47.420
I guess so. I think I started liking you then.

00:51:48.230 --> 00:51:49.630
My goodness.

00:51:55.170 --> 00:51:57.170
- Hurry and eat. - Okay.

00:51:57.270 --> 00:51:58.270
I'm heading out.

00:52:01.810 --> 00:52:02.970
Stay while I eat.

00:52:05.840 --> 00:52:06.910
I don't want to eat alone.

00:52:21.190 --> 00:52:25.100
There's no point in going there if you just drive me back.

00:52:26.600 --> 00:52:27.900
But what am I supposed to do?

00:52:28.730 --> 00:52:29.870
I can't let you go home by yourself.

00:52:41.210 --> 00:52:42.680
I didn't know I'd be like this.

00:52:49.390 --> 00:52:50.390
I'm leaving now.

00:52:52.120 --> 00:52:53.720
I'll walk you to the corner.

00:53:40.770 --> 00:53:41.770
Su Bin.

00:53:49.480 --> 00:53:51.750
Kim Seok. What are you doing here?

00:53:54.320 --> 00:53:57.290
- Who's that? - A guy I dated in college.

00:53:58.890 --> 00:54:00.460
My ex, actually.

00:54:00.860 --> 00:54:02.289
He found my YouTube and wouldn't stop calling,

00:54:02.290 --> 00:54:04.460
so I blocked him. I guess he borrowed someone's phone.

00:54:06.860 --> 00:54:07.860
So, he's that punk.

00:54:09.900 --> 00:54:11.130
Are you Su Bin's oldest brother?

00:54:11.740 --> 00:54:12.940
I've heard so much about you.

00:54:13.470 --> 00:54:15.770
No, he's not. He's my boyfriend.

00:54:16.140 --> 00:54:17.140
Boyfriend?

00:54:21.950 --> 00:54:22.950
Hey, Lee Su Bin.

00:54:23.750 --> 00:54:25.080
Why are you going out with some old man?

00:54:27.780 --> 00:54:28.790
"Old man?"

00:54:30.890 --> 00:54:32.420
Oh, so you're rich.

00:54:34.190 --> 00:54:36.290
- Is that why you're with him? - You little...

00:54:37.660 --> 00:54:38.700
Are you crazy?

00:54:39.060 --> 00:54:41.500
- Hey. - Who are you to say that?

00:54:41.830 --> 00:54:44.400
- Do you ever look in the mirror? - There's a huge age gap.

00:54:44.900 --> 00:54:47.100
Hey, you. What is your problem?

00:54:47.470 --> 00:54:50.110
When someone says no, it means no. Why do you keep hanging around?

00:54:51.170 --> 00:54:53.910
And you've been calling her from unknown numbers, haven't you?

00:54:54.610 --> 00:54:56.180
And now, you're showing up at her home?

00:54:56.650 --> 00:54:58.420
This is stalking!

00:54:59.450 --> 00:55:00.450
Unbelievable.

00:55:02.620 --> 00:55:03.850
All right, that's it.

00:55:05.060 --> 00:55:06.790
You're coming with me to the police station. Let's go.

00:55:07.390 --> 00:55:09.430
- Okay, fine. - Let's go.

00:55:09.490 --> 00:55:10.830
Okay! I'll stay away.

00:55:11.800 --> 00:55:15.370
- But I thought Su Bin was single... - Well, she isn't anymore!

00:55:16.370 --> 00:55:18.440
Lee Su Bin. What do you want me to do?

00:55:21.910 --> 00:55:22.910
Just let him go.

00:55:25.540 --> 00:55:30.080
You. Apologise to her. Apologise for harassing her.

00:55:32.580 --> 00:55:35.650
- I'm sorry for harassing you. - And promise you won't contact her.

00:55:36.920 --> 00:55:38.160
I'll never contact you again.

00:55:43.390 --> 00:55:45.360
Like you said, this old guy has a lot of money.

00:55:46.360 --> 00:55:47.830
If I see you bothering her one more time,

00:55:48.300 --> 00:55:50.230
I'll make your life very difficult. Got it?

00:55:51.470 --> 00:55:52.900
- Yes. - Louder!

00:55:53.400 --> 00:55:55.210
- Yes! - Now, leave.

00:55:59.840 --> 00:56:00.840
Stop.

00:56:01.580 --> 00:56:02.910
Aren't you going to say goodbye to her?

00:56:08.850 --> 00:56:09.850
What?

00:56:19.760 --> 00:56:20.760
Hey.

00:56:21.670 --> 00:56:23.370
When did you get so cool?

00:56:28.270 --> 00:56:29.510
Isn't that why you fell for me?

00:56:30.070 --> 00:56:31.070
No.

00:56:31.710 --> 00:56:33.110
Then why did you?

00:56:33.380 --> 00:56:34.480
Because you're an old man?

00:56:35.150 --> 00:56:36.180
What?

00:56:37.750 --> 00:56:38.750
What?

00:56:39.320 --> 00:56:41.550
I'll tell you why later. My mom will be worried.

00:56:41.950 --> 00:56:43.650
Bye. Drive safe.

00:56:44.860 --> 00:56:46.590
Wait, hey...

00:56:52.700 --> 00:56:54.260
I'm so worried, it's driving me crazy.

00:56:55.930 --> 00:56:57.170
She's just too pretty.

00:57:11.880 --> 00:57:13.120
Is it because of my clothes?

00:57:14.750 --> 00:57:15.750
Yes, that's it.

00:57:16.320 --> 00:57:18.860
It's the clothes. The clothes are the problem.

00:57:34.100 --> 00:57:36.040
My clothes are all too classy.

00:57:41.110 --> 00:57:43.050
I wonder if Woo Jin left any of his clothes here.

00:57:46.520 --> 00:57:47.680
Come to think of it,

00:57:48.050 --> 00:57:49.850
I haven't talked to Woo Jin at all lately.

00:57:54.190 --> 00:57:56.090
I just don't understand you at all.

00:57:56.430 --> 00:58:00.060
We're lucky your fever went down. Why climb the hospital roof so late?

00:58:00.600 --> 00:58:03.800
What? Was it easy to go up but too hard to jump?

00:58:04.270 --> 00:58:05.540
You couldn't take that final step, could you?

00:58:06.000 --> 00:58:08.670
That's what it means to be human. That's what life is.

00:58:09.040 --> 00:58:11.710
Life is something you only get once. When it's gone, it's all gone.

00:58:18.450 --> 00:58:20.780
For months, she was so incredibly nice to me,

00:58:21.420 --> 00:58:22.890
and I really grew to like her.

00:58:23.520 --> 00:58:25.490
I really liked her.

00:58:26.320 --> 00:58:28.990
Pull yourself together. You need to focus on staying alive.

00:58:29.260 --> 00:58:32.000
Unless you actually want to die, you'd better take care of yourself.

00:58:36.500 --> 00:58:37.900
And what if I do?

00:58:40.770 --> 00:58:42.540
Don't you remember what I told you?

00:58:43.540 --> 00:58:45.380
I told you. You don't get to die.

00:58:46.810 --> 00:58:48.710
Who gave you permission to die?

00:58:52.920 --> 00:58:54.850
How dare she refuse to donate her liver?

00:59:05.700 --> 00:59:07.500
Why is everyone so weak?

00:59:07.960 --> 00:59:09.670
They can't even stick it out to the end.

00:59:16.670 --> 00:59:18.240
What's this warning light for?

00:59:22.650 --> 00:59:23.850
It's the transmission warning light.

00:59:24.150 --> 00:59:26.080
Let me check the oil line underneath.

00:59:32.820 --> 00:59:35.260
You're saying this is a tracking device?

00:59:35.460 --> 00:59:37.990
Yes. It was attached near the rear wheel.

00:59:46.140 --> 00:59:48.300
So Ri likes Dokgo Chan too, you know.

00:59:49.340 --> 00:59:51.340
So who's supposed to make the first move?

00:59:53.940 --> 00:59:56.880
They're pulled together and will kiss at the same time.

00:59:57.750 --> 01:00:00.480
So that's how it works?

01:00:00.550 --> 01:00:02.620
(Take My Heart)

01:00:04.420 --> 01:00:05.820
But still,

01:00:06.190 --> 01:00:09.360
shouldn't Dokgo Chan be the one to cup the back of her head first?

01:00:10.590 --> 01:00:11.590
Like this?

01:00:12.460 --> 01:00:16.630
No. Hey, who kisses like that?

01:00:16.730 --> 01:00:18.600
Hey, you need to set the mood.

01:00:19.840 --> 01:00:20.870
How?

01:00:23.670 --> 01:00:24.910
Watch me, Yeong Ra.

01:00:28.550 --> 01:00:31.850
First, you gaze deeply into each other's eyes.

01:00:34.820 --> 01:00:38.220
Then you both lean in at the same time.

01:00:41.490 --> 01:00:42.490
Like this?

01:00:43.590 --> 01:00:46.800
And right about now, you cup her head...

01:01:04.650 --> 01:01:05.820
What do you two think you're doing?

01:01:10.320 --> 01:01:11.690
You! Get out.

01:01:12.360 --> 01:01:15.390
- Let me just explain... - Didn't you hear me? Get out!

01:01:24.330 --> 01:01:25.770
I'm not leaving...

01:01:26.340 --> 01:01:27.740
Yeong Ra here alone.

01:01:28.840 --> 01:01:29.840
What did you just say?

01:01:33.280 --> 01:01:34.510
Go wait outside.

01:01:35.280 --> 01:01:36.280
No, I mean,

01:01:37.010 --> 01:01:38.180
please just wait outside.

01:01:41.920 --> 01:01:42.920
All right.

01:02:01.970 --> 01:02:04.970
I knew you were up to something when you played innocent for your dad.

01:02:08.580 --> 01:02:09.780
So this is what it was all about.

01:02:10.510 --> 01:02:12.220
He's the jerk who's been filling your head with nonsense.

01:02:12.850 --> 01:02:13.920
What do I do?

01:02:14.750 --> 01:02:16.750
What am I going to do?

01:02:18.290 --> 01:02:21.520
So he's the reason you refused to be physically intimate.

01:02:22.460 --> 01:02:24.930
And you had the nerve to pull that act for your father?

01:02:26.900 --> 01:02:29.100
Your father will be thrilled when he finds out, won't he?

01:02:32.440 --> 01:02:33.700
He's fired. Effective immediately.

01:02:35.040 --> 01:02:36.440
You can't do that, Mom.

01:02:37.710 --> 01:02:38.710
What?

01:02:41.480 --> 01:02:42.480
If you do that, then I...

01:02:43.580 --> 01:02:45.320
have something I need to tell Dad.

01:02:48.620 --> 01:02:49.750
About Woo Jin.

01:02:55.690 --> 01:02:56.690
What about Woo Jin?

01:02:59.130 --> 01:03:01.000
The fact that Woo Jin is trying to get a liver transplant.

01:03:02.830 --> 01:03:04.130
Should I go ahead and tell Dad about that?

01:03:46.610 --> 01:03:49.010
(Our Golden Days)

01:03:49.450 --> 01:03:53.480
This is the first money I've earned all by myself. I made my own money!

01:03:53.650 --> 01:03:56.620
You want me to model in a fashion show?

01:03:56.790 --> 01:03:59.620
You shouldn't try to haggle with the designated driver.

01:03:59.690 --> 01:04:00.790
Come on.

01:04:02.660 --> 01:04:06.700
Wait, so you took the money? Are you out of your mind?

01:04:06.830 --> 01:04:08.600
Let's keep it a secret from your sister.

01:04:08.670 --> 01:04:11.030
I'm hiding your liver transplant, and she dares to use it against me?

01:04:11.100 --> 01:04:12.940
If Chairman Park Jin Seok finds out I have a secret daughter,

01:04:13.000 --> 01:04:15.570
- what do you think he'd do to me? - Since you're going to die anyway,

01:04:15.910 --> 01:04:18.880
stop playing games with your life when you don't have the guts for it.